            <ArticleTitle>Agelamasines A and B, diterpene alkaloids from an Okinawan marine sponge Agelas sp.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11418-017-1157-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two new diterpene alkaloids having an N-methyladenine moiety, agelamasines A (1) and B (2), were isolated from an Okinawan marine sponge Agelas sp. The structures of 1 and 2 were elucidated on the basis of spectroscopic analyses. Agelamasine A (1) is the first diterpene alkaloid with a rearranged (4 → 2)-abeo-clerodane skeleton from a marine source, while agelamasine B (2) is a clerodane diterpene alkaloid.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
